SUMMARY:Sprints at Priory
DESCRIPTION:Leader: Joe de la Mata\n\nFun running session starting with a q
 uick warmup + 10-20min set of sprints + 3K easy-pace recovery run + 10-20mi
 n set of sprints + cool-down stretches.\n\nSprints sets: this will be a set
  of exercises in pairs or teams of 3 (depending on the numbers). One person
  will be sprinting towards some markers (trees/lamp posts) and back while t
 heir pals will be doing some exercises for active recovery before swapping 
 over.\n\nSounds intense? Don’t panic! Do it at your own pace. This sessio
 n will be adapted to everyone’s abilities and adapted exercises will be o
 ffered when needed.\n\nMeeting point: Priory Park (by the Splash)\n\nMeetin
 g time: 6.30pm\n\nDuration: ~1hr\n\nKit: high-vis clothing and head-torches
  recommended.\n\nLiRF: Joe - [Phone Number Redacted]\n\nView on Strava: htt
 ps://www.strava.com/clubs/208705/group_events/3465046689168388988\n\nSynced
  from Strava Club 208705 on Sat\, 7 Mar @ 4:44 PM
